# with -L it counts a directory again each time a link leads to it, and a link that leads nowhere as the link, without an error; the standard counts a file with more than one link (a directory has at least two) once, and says that du reports an error when it cannot stat a file
-aHL t
-aL t
-H -L t
-HkL
-kL
-L t
-sL t
-H t/dang
-L t/dang
# with -a it writes the second name of a file with two links, with size 0; the standard says it is counted and written for one entry only
-a
-a h
-ak
-ak h
-ax
# a repeated option is an error there (clap)
-a -a
-k -k
-s -s
-x -x
# it takes an option after an operand; POSIX08 treats it as an operand (PCTS du 16)
t/c -a
t/c -s t/a
